WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.061 --> 00:00:04.663
Once there was a fox who liked to play tricks.

2
00:00:04.664 --> 00:00:09.058
He especially liked to play tricks on his neighbor, a stork.

3
00:00:09.059 --> 00:00:13.955
"That stork is funny looking," the fox thought.

4
00:00:13.956 --> 00:00:16.736
"Her legs are so tall.

5
00:00:16.737 --> 00:00:22.782
And her bill is useless—it's too long and pointy!"

6
00:00:22.783 --> 00:00:26.834
One day the fox got an idea for a new trick.

7
00:00:26.835 --> 00:00:33.811
"Stork!" The fox waved, carefully hiding his sly smile.

8
00:00:33.812 --> 00:00:38.219
"Please come to my house for dinner tonight.

9
00:00:38.220 --> 00:00:43.587
I'll prepare a delicious meal for us."

10
00:00:43.588 --> 00:00:50.347
"Why, thank you, Fox," the stork said. "I'd love to come."

11
00:00:50.348 --> 00:00:54.512
At dinnertime the stork knocked on the fox's door.

12
00:00:54.513 --> 00:00:58.975
"I'm looking forward to this meal," she thought.

13
00:00:58.976 --> 00:01:07.005
"I wonder what Fox has prepared for us."

14
00:01:07.006 --> 00:01:14.680
The fox greeted the stork and led her to the table.

15
00:01:14.681 --> 00:01:19.565
Then he set out two shallow dishes of soup.

16
00:01:19.566 --> 00:01:23.356
The fox eagerly slurped up his soup.

17
00:01:23.357 --> 00:01:27.759
But the poor stork stared at her dish and frowned.

18
00:01:27.760 --> 00:01:32.372
"I can't sip this soup!" she thought.

19
00:01:32.373 --> 00:01:35.719
"My bill is too long."

20
00:01:35.720 --> 00:01:40.563
The fox pretended not to notice that the stork was having trouble.

21
00:01:40.564 --> 00:01:46.216
He slurped his soup noisily.

22
00:01:46.217 --> 00:01:53.528
"Yum! This is so delicious!" he said.

23
00:01:53.529 --> 00:01:57.699
Suddenly the stork realized something.

24
00:01:57.700 --> 00:02:03.220
"Fox is playing a trick on me again!" she thought.

25
00:02:03.221 --> 00:02:06.653
But the stork was a very calm bird.

26
00:02:06.654 --> 00:02:09.409
She didn't get angry.

27
00:02:09.410 --> 00:02:14.923
Instead she got a clever idea.

28
00:02:14.924 --> 00:02:20.279
A few days later, the stork hurried over to the fox.

29
00:02:20.280 --> 00:02:25.209
"It's my turn to invite you for dinner," the stork said.

30
00:02:25.210 --> 00:02:28.701
"Please join me for a meal tonight.

31
00:02:28.702 --> 00:02:32.869
I'll prepare a delicious meal for us."

32
00:02:32.870 --> 00:02:36.939
"Wonderful!" the fox said.

33
00:02:36.940 --> 00:02:39.859
The fox arrived right on time.

34
00:02:39.860 --> 00:02:44.797
As he stepped inside, he sniffed the air.

35
00:02:44.798 --> 00:02:51.230
"Mmm! You made fish—my favorite meal!"

36
00:02:51.231 --> 00:03:01.078
"Yes." The stork smiled and set two tall, narrow jars on the table. "Enjoy!"

37
00:03:01.079 --> 00:03:04.725
The stork happily poked her bill into her jar.

38
00:03:04.726 --> 00:03:07.639
She pulled out some fish.

39
00:03:07.640 --> 00:03:11.652
The fox stared at his jar in confusion.

40
00:03:11.653 --> 00:03:15.419
"How will I eat this?" he thought.

41
00:03:15.420 --> 00:03:20.403
The fox tried to fit his mouth into the jar.

42
00:03:20.404 --> 00:03:22.987
But the opening was much too narrow.

43
00:03:22.988 --> 00:03:28.093
Meanwhile the stork was eating easily, using her long bill.

44
00:03:28.094 --> 00:03:32.898
Finally the fox stood up, tossing his napkin on the table.

45
00:03:32.899 --> 00:03:38.272
"You're a very rude host!"

46
00:03:38.273 --> 00:03:41.277
The stork smiled calmly.

47
00:03:41.278 --> 00:03:45.202
"I can see you're upset, Fox.

48
00:03:45.203 --> 00:03:48.955
Maybe it will teach you something important.

49
00:03:48.956 --> 00:03:56.801
You should treat others the way you want to be treated!"

